                    <item name="Size" type_name="gh_single" type_code="5">9</item>
                    <item name="Text" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">STEP 1  -  Split the skin into a grid
Goal: a grid of UV domains: panels around × floors up.
Idea: Every surface has its own UV coordinates. Divide Domain²
   cuts that UV square into U × V cells without touching the
   geometry yet.
Watch for: V = Floors, so each row of panels is one storey.
Wire check: panels around -&gt; U, Floors -&gt; V.</item>
                  </items>
